  "title": "Majority vote",
  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.sum-of-products"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "Three sensors on the boiler each say “too hot”, and one could be faulty, so the cut-out trips when at least two agree: AB + BC + AC. Three ANDs (IC1) feed two ORs (IC2). One AND and one OR input aren’t wired yet.",
    "goal": "Finish the wiring so TRIP lights when two or three of A, B, C are on.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Majority of three",
      "rows": [
        [
          "IC1 74HC08",
          "A·B → pin 3 · B·C → pin 6 · A·C → pin 8"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 74HC32",
          "(A·B + B·C) → pin 3 · then + A·C → pin 6"
        ],
        [
          "Missing",
          "C into gate 3, and gate 3’s output into IC2 pin 5"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Each pair of sensors gets its own AND, then the three results are ORed together. Gate 3 of IC1 is A·C: its inputs are pin 9 (column 8, bottom, already A) and pin 10 (column 7, bottom).",
    "Pin 10 needs C (C is column 7, top half): a wire across the gap, column 7 top to column 7 bottom. Gate 3’s output is pin 8, column 9 bottom; it goes to IC2 pin 5, column 21.",
    "Two wires: column 7 top → column 7 bottom (C into pin 10), and column 9 bottom → column 21 top (A·C into the second OR)."
  ],
